faqs.a:
The following are prohibited at the reservoir:
(1)
Swimming, wading, tubing, belly boating, floating on a flotation device, windsurfing,
                  and scuba diving;
(2)
Possession, use, or being under the influence of alcohol or controlled substances;
(3)
Possession of glass beverage containers;
(4)
Horses, dogs, other pets, motorcycles, or motorbikes, except that dogs shall be permitted
                  in the following areas:
a.
Arvada Dog Park, located north of 64th Avenue Community Trail and southeast of the
                  southernmost spillway structure at Arvada/Blunn Reservoir;
b.
Arvada Disc Golf Course Park, located north of 64th Avenue Community Trail and east
                  of the southernmost spillway structure at Arvada/Blunn Reservoir;
(5)
Boats with gasoline motors;
(6)
Shore fishing from the dam, spillway, or wildlife areas;
(7)
Boat fishing in the wildlife area or at other areas marked with buoys;
(8)
Ice fishing or ice skating;
(9)
Possession or use of firearms, bows and arrows, or airguns;
(10)
Hunting or trapping;
(11)
Dumping of trash;
(12)
Camping;
(13)
Open fires;
(14)
Fishing or coming within 50 feet of the small ponds located south of the reservoir;
(15)
Possession or use of fireworks;
(16)
Digging, trenching, or excavating; and
(17)
Driving vehicles on any area, except the entrance road or parking lot.
(Code 1981, § 22-23; Ord. No. 2577, § 2, 12-19-1988; Ord. No. 2956, § 5, 2-15-1993;
               Ord. No. 3844, § 2, 12-15-2003)
